ep9: third-party code in this repository

ep9's own code is licensed under "MIT OR Apache-2.0" (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE).
This file lists source code that is copied or ported into this repository from
other projects. That code keeps its own licence, given below with each entry.
ep9 has no NOTICE file. Third-party notices live here, so Apache-2.0 section 4(d)
adds no duty for the users of ep9's own code.

Not listed here:
- Cargo dependencies (crates.io). Release builds ship a notice file that
  cargo-about generates from Cargo.lock (docs/plan/12-governance.md section 1).
- Checkouts that scripts/sync-*.sh fetch into third_party/<name>/ (git-ignored).
  They are not part of this repository and ep9 binaries do not contain them.

Rules (docs/plan/12-governance.md section 1):
- The PR that copies or ports third-party code adds its entry here.
- Each copied or ported file keeps the original copyright and licence lines and
  adds the line "Ported for ep9 from <project> <path> at <commit>".
- The full licence text of each project follows its entry, once per project.
- No crate in this repository adds its own NOTICE file.

